  "notes": [
   "Required Core is headed 'SELECT TWO (6 UNITS)' but printed as two 'or' pairs (PHILOS 009 or PHILOS 006; PHILOS 001 or PHILOS 020); recorded as a required block of two entries with alternatives, i.e. one course from each pair.",
   "List A also allows 'Any Required Core not already used' (PHILOS 009/006/001/020); List B also allows 'Any List A course not already used'; List C also allows 'Any List A or B course not already used.' These cross-references are not duplicated as courses in the later blocks.",
   "Catalog prints codes with leading zeros (e.g. PHILOS 009, FRENCH 003); these match closed-list codes without zeros (PHILOS 9, FRENCH 3), so not marked as additions. FRENCH 003 is printed as 'Intermediate French' vs closed-list 'INTERMEDIATE FRENCH I'.",
   "ge_units recorded as the 34 semester units stated for Cal-GETC in the requirements text; the totals table separately prints 'Additional Cal-GETC Requirement* 22-28' (not including 6-12 double-countable major units).",
   "degree_elective_units taken from 'Additional CSU-Transferable Units 12-20'; degree_total from 'Total Units 60'.",
   "Students with catalog rights prior to Fall 2025 may follow CSU GE Breadth or IGETC instead of Cal-GETC."
